      "message": "go/android-api-guidelines#framework-rethrow-remoteexception\n\nAlthough this isn\u0027t calling into the system service, the general pattern used elsewhere is to call [e.reThrowAsRuntimeException](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/RemoteException.java;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d63?q\u003dRemoteException\u0026ct\u003dos\u0026sq\u003dgit:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain@main\u0026gsn\u003drethrowAsRuntimeException\u0026gs\u003dKYTHE%3A%2F%2Fkythe%3A%2F%2Fgoogleplex-android.googlesource.com%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2Fmain%3Flang%3Djava%3Fpath%3Dandroid.os.RemoteException%2340bee8001623f896e3b35718cb1523205b23f2487982045dd67c8f85ecbbc2a0) rather than absorbing the remote exception.  A remote exception would be a fatal error and it would be better for the caller to know rather than silently absorbing the exception and returning an empty list (go/android-api-guidelines#return-error).  I suspect a remote exception would be a fatal error so there is likely no need to return a specific exception or error code here?",
